Developer Guide
===============

Eclipse
-------

Following the initial checkout, or after updating dependencies in the Build.scala file, run:

  play "eclipse with-source=true"


Assets
------

When updating the bootstrap.js file, concatenate the "Modals", "Dropdowns", "Toggleable tabs" and the "Typeahead" plugins, 
and append the bootstrap-fileupload, bootstrap-datepicker and bootstrap-timepicker plugins.

When updating angular-custom.js, append angular-route and angular-sanitize. Remove any "//# sourceMappingURL" lines.

When updating highcharts.js, append highcharts-more.


SSL Trust Store
---------------

Netatmo's SSL certificate is issued by StartCom. The StartCom root certificate is included in Ubuntu's OpenJDK package, but not in Oracle's.  

To add the certificate, download it from https://www.startssl.com/certs/ca.pem, and run:

  keytool -import -trustcacerts -keystore /etc/ssl/certs/java/cacerts -storepass changeit -noprompt -alias startcom.ca -file ca.pem 


Tests
-----

To run a single test:
  
  play "test-only com.zenobase.testing.BrowserTest"

To run all tests except Selenium tests:

  play -Dwebdriver.enabled=false test


Release Procedure
-----------------

  1. Push the code to the build server. This should trigger a build.

  2. Obtain the build number [CloudBees].

  3. Edit the "Custom JSON" field for the "Production" stack [OpsWorks]:

     3.1. Set play.build to the new build number.

     3.2. (if migrating) Set elasticsearch.replay to the previous clusterName and increment clusterName.

  4. Set up new instances [OpsWorks]:

     4.1. Add two m3.medium instances named "{build number}-1a" in us-east-1a and "{build number}-1c" in us-east-1c to the "Elasticsearch" layer.

     4.2. (if migrating) Add an m1.xlarge instance named "{build number}-1d" in us-east-1d to the "Elasticsearch" layer.

     4.3. Add the new instances to the "Play" layer.

  5. Before proceeding:
  
     5.1. The build must complete [CloudBees].

     5.2. There should be no traffic [Google Analytics].

     5.3. The status check must show 4 nodes and green health [/status].

  6. Start either the new m3.large instance (if migrating) or the new m3.medium instances [OpsWorks].

  7. Add all new instance(s) to the load balancer, and remove all old instances as soon as one of the new instances is listed as "in service" [AWS Console].

  8. (if migrating) Start the two m3.medium instances as well [OpsWorks].

  9. Wait for the status check to show 6 (if migrating) or 8 (if not migrating) nodes and green health [/status].

  10. Stop the m1.xlarge instance (if migrating) as well as any old instances [OpsWorks].

  11. Wait for 4 nodes and green health [/status].

  12. Set the "keep this build forever" flag [CloudBees].

  13. Move the "prod" tag to HEAD.

  14. Cleanup (optional):

      14.1. Remove stopped instances [OpsWorks].

      14.2. Remove the "keep this build forever" flag from builds older than a month or so [CloudBees].

      14.3. Remove instances that are no longer reporting data [New Relic].

      14.4. (if migrating) Remove all but the last few S3 buckets [AWS Console].
